-- **Step:** Stage 1: Jointly train triplanes and MLP on a subset of 500 randomly selected shapes. Use a batch size of 1 object per iteration and 500k occupancy values points per object. Train for 200 epochs with a learning rate of 1e-3 [S4]. Stage 2: Freeze the shared MLP. Train triplane features for each object individually using a batch size of 200k occupancy values per object. Train for 30 epochs with a learning rate of 1e-3 [S4].
-- **Parameter:** Triplane feature dimension: $128 \times 128 \times 32 \times 3$. Triplane initialization: values drawn from a normal distribution with standard deviation 0.1. MLP architecture: Fourier feature mapping layer (scale factor 1) followed by 3 fully connected layers of dimension 128, each with ReLU activation [S4].
